The recorded runs that tests/expected.sh checks gcon-vm against: for
each program, NAME.out (standard output) and NAME.err (standard error,
then "status N"), or NAME.skip with the reason it is not checked.

They were recorded from Gcon's Go VM on 2026-11-26 (with a mode of
tests/expected.sh since removed), while it was the reference, before its
retirement; ACCEPTED lists the programs recorded from gcon-vm instead,
by decision. A program is skipped if Gcon cannot build it, if it does
not finish within 10 seconds, if two runs differed, or if its output
depends on the machine (host name, user, environment) or the clock
(dates, times, randomize): those were found by reading the programs
and their output, not only by running them twice.

New programs are recorded from gcon-vm (tests/expected.sh -accept), once
their runs are checked against iconx.
